<ol class="text-fg-muted list-decimal space-y-4 pl-5 text-sm">
  <li>
    Open AIS-catcher's control panel. If you already see <strong>Output</strong>
    , continue below. From the web viewer, use <strong>Control</strong> when
    available. In older versions, click the toolbox icon at the top left,
    labeled <strong>System and receiver statistics</strong>, then scroll to the
    bottom and click <strong>System</strong>.
    <p class="mt-2">
      If neither control is available, open your{" "}
      <a href="https://jvde-github.github.io/AIS-catcher-docs/managed/dashboard/">
        managed-mode dashboard
      </a>{" "}
      (normally <code>http://localhost:8118</code> on the receiver's computer),
      or use our Command line instructions for your existing setup.
    </p>
  </li>
  <li>
    Choose <strong>Output → MQTT → Add</strong> (or{" "}
    <strong>Add MQTT output</strong>) and paste your Open Waters MQTT URL into{" "}
    <strong>URL</strong>.
    <slot />
  </li>
  <li>
    Open <strong>Advanced settings</strong> and set{" "}
    <strong>Message Format</strong> to <strong>NMEA</strong>. The default JSON
    format does not work with this output.
  </li>
  <li>
    Keep the output <strong>Active</strong>, save it, and apply the changes or
    restart the receiver if prompted. Return to the Open Waters token page to
    check reception.
  </li>
</ol>
